  "scout_brief": "Focus: observability & reporting \u2014 logging, metrics (/metrics, Prometheus), operator-facing reporting (daily-report, marker/corpus-version reporting). MOTIVATING BUG: ingest/store.py::write_chunks writes corpus-version.json with chunk_count=len(chunks)/paper_count from only the LAST per-paper batch (bulk_ingest + re_embed call it once per paper) -> notebook markers read chunk_count=106 while the real table has 10298 rows; a ~100x silent discrepancy NOTHING flagged (surfaced only by manual inspection during the live cutover). Scout for capabilities that make this CLASS of bug \u2014 a persisted metadata field silently diverging from ground truth, wrong values in startup logs/reports going unnoticed \u2014 easy to catch automatically: invariant/consistency checks at write or startup (marker counts vs table row count), structured logging with assertable fields, metrics exposing ground-truth-vs-recorded deltas, a reporting/diff surface, drift/regression alarms. Bias toward LOCAL-FIRST, single-workstation, no-new-heavy-infra options.",
